# Generated from: specs/14-establish-production-readiness-and-anonymous-abuse-controls/requirements.md
Feature: Establish local runtime safety and anonymous abuse controls
  As a group maintainer
  I want local runtime health, schema changes, and anonymous endpoints to fail safely
  So that I can verify the service without hidden local infrastructure or abuse-control risk

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Local readiness is database-aware while liveness remains process-only
    Given the local Web process exposes /health and /health/ready
    And the local Web process is serving
    When local PostgreSQL is unavailable
    Then /health reports the serving process as live
    And /health/ready reports the database-dependent service as unhealthy

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Local migrate-only applies schema without listening
    Given a local release contains a pending EF Core migration
    When the Web executable runs with --migrate-only
    Then one non-serving process applies the pending migration and exits successfully
    And no HTTP port is bound by the migrate-only process

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Ordinary local Web startup never migrates
    Given the database is available to the local Web process
    When the Web process starts without --migrate-only
    Then it serves normally
    And it does not apply schema migrations

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Local Compose completes migration before Web starts
    Given local Docker Compose starts PostgreSQL, migration, and Web services
    When the stack starts
    Then PostgreSQL becomes healthy before migration runs
    And the one-shot migration service completes successfully before Web starts
    And a migration failure prevents Web startup

  @SCN005
  Scenario Outline: Excess anonymous traffic is rejected without state change
    Given one client IP has exhausted the <tier> limit
    And matching valid and invalid route identifiers exist
    When that client sends another valid request and another invalid request
    Then both responses are HTTP 429
    And both responses contain the same generic retry text and retry guidance
    And neither request executes a page handler or changes workflow or token state

    Examples:
      | tier                        |
      | request mutation            |
      | private-token read         |
      | assignment-action mutation |

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Local allowlist permits two identities independently
    Given two distinct identities are locally allowlisted
    And a third identity is not locally allowlisted
    When each identity signs in independently
    Then both allowlisted identities can access coordinator behavior
    And the third identity remains unauthorized
    And no production OIDC handoff is required

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Local verification covers the corrected scope
    Given the local runtime, Compose, health, migration, authorization, and limiter behavior is implemented
    When the focused local verification runs
    Then it covers readiness and liveness
    And it covers migrate-only and ordinary-startup behavior
    And it covers Compose sequencing, independent per-IP limiter tiers, generic throttling without mutation, and two allowlisted identities
